00:46:54.638 --> 00:47:05.907
So, we say that the quadratic form is equal to -1
 on the only basic vector in the space V.

00:47:05.907 --> 00:47:12.967
And then, of course, we get that this multiplication corresponds to the multiplication of complex numbers,

00:47:12.967 --> 00:47:18.598
and the basic vector e₁ corresponds to the imaginary unit " i ".

00:47:18.598 --> 00:47:25.631
We could take the Clifford algebra in a two-dimensional space R²

00:47:25.631 --> 00:47:34.554
with the ordinary Euclidean scalar product, where eᵢ ∘ eᵢ = 1, not -1.

00:47:34.554 --> 00:47:39.288
